======================================================================
(E5) two boundaries (coverage-adjudication axis for genm-l2engine)
======================================================================
  n=2: best-case max corank-d=1 (PATH d>=2? False); binding-atom d-values=[0, 1] (COVER d>=2 atom? False)
  n=3: best-case max corank-d=1 (PATH d>=2? False); binding-atom d-values=[1] (COVER d>=2 atom? False)
  n=4: best-case max corank-d=1 (PATH d>=2? False); binding-atom d-values=[1, 2] (COVER d>=2 atom? True)
  n=5: best-case max corank-d=2 (PATH d>=2? True); binding-atom d-values=[1, 2] (COVER d>=2 atom? True)
  n=6: best-case max corank-d=2 (PATH d>=2? True); binding-atom d-values=[2] (COVER d>=2 atom? True)
  n=7: best-case max corank-d=2 (PATH d>=2? True); binding-atom d-values=[2, 3] (COVER d>=2 atom? True)
  n=8: best-case max corank-d=3 (PATH d>=2? True); binding-atom d-values=[2, 3] (COVER d>=2 atom? True)
  => PATH boundary (no all-d<=1 optimal path) = n=5
  => COVER boundary (a binding d>=2 atom exists) = n=4
(E5) VERDICT  PATH boundary = 5 and COVER boundary = 4 (both exact): True
     [adjudication for genm-l2engine: a resolution covers all binding rank strata,
      so COVER (n>=4) is operative unless the d>=2 binding chart resolves natively --
      W1 says single-factor blow-ups do not principalize it. This witness states the
      two boundaries; it does not choose the cover.]

